„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒAnd the LORD said to Samuel, Behold, I will do a thing in Israel, at which both the ears of every one that heareth it shall tingle.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚In that day I will perform against Eli all things which I have spoken concerning his house: when I begin, I will also make an end.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFor I have told him that I will judge his house for ever for the iniquity which he knoweth; because his sons made themselves vile, and he restrained them not.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒAnd therefore I have sworn unto the house of Eli, that the iniquity of Eli's house shall not be purged with sacrifice nor offering for ever.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzAnd Samuel lay until the morning, and opened the doors of the house of the LORD. And Samuel feared to shew Eli the vision.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMThen Eli called Samuel, and said, Samuel, my son. And he answered, Here am I.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÍAnd he said, What is the thing that the LORD hath said unto thee? I pray thee hide it not from me: God do so to thee, and more also, if thou hide any thing from me of all the things that he said unto thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxAnd Samuel told him every whit, and hid nothing from him. And he said, It is the LORD: let him do what seemeth him good.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]And Samuel grew, and the LORD was with him, and did let none of his words fall to the ground.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhAnd all Israel from Dan even to Beer-sheba knew that Samuel was established to be a prophet of the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqAnd the LORD appeared again in Shiloh: for the LORD revealed himself to Samuel in Shiloh by the word of the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse